 "title": "Arabic comma: space moved but not re-added after ، (words glued)",
 "description": "**Bug (reported from a real subtitle file):** Satr removes the space *before* the Arabic comma but never adds one *after* it, so words get glued together.\n\nInput cue:\n```\n1\n00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000\nهذا رائع ،أليس كذلك\n```\nAfter `satr fix`: `هذا رائع،أليس كذلك` — viewers read «رائع،أليس» as one word.\nExpected: `هذا رائع، أليس كذلك` (no space before ، / ؛ / ؟, one space after when a letter follows).\n\nAlso: the CLI prints `0 fixes applied` even though it changed the line.",
